spans.s:
√bhañj (bhanákti; babháñja; ábhāṅkṣīt;
bhaṅkṣyáti; bhagná [957c]; bhaṅktvā́;
-bhájya). break. [opinions are
divided as to whether √√bhañj, 2bhuj,
and bhām (see these) orig. began w. bhr-;
cf giri-bhráj, ‘breaking forth from the
mountains’: if bhañj does stand for
*bhrañj, then Lat. frangere, ‘break,’
nau-frag-a, ‘ship-breaking’ (tempestas),
and Ger. brechen, Eng. break are akin.]
